# Auto-resolve package-lock.json merge conflicts.
#
# Background: this fork tracks an upstream that periodically bumps frontend
# dependencies via Dependabot. Each upstream merge produced a conflict in
# package-lock.json that humans cannot resolve by hand (it's a 250KB
# generated file with cross-referenced integrity hashes). The repeated
# workaround — deleting and regenerating the lockfile — silently re-rolled
# every caret-ranged transitive dependency to whatever the public npm
# registry happened to offer that day, which broke production on Jun 1.
#
# This merge driver (registered per-clone by frontend/package.json's
# `prepare` script via the `npm-merge-driver` package) reconciles
# package-lock.json by taking upstream's side and running `npm install`
# against the merged package.json. Result: conflicts disappear and every
# pin that wasn't touched by either side stays exactly where it was.
package-lock.json merge=npm-merge-driver
